design\activity\card__5cdae748-9597-4d29-8dc0-3d4b5df3aa7f.json:4187:          "content": "Recommend `@tanstack/react-virtual`.\n\nWhy:\n\n- Headless. Keeps existing MUI `Paper`, `List`, `ListItemButton`, ARIA, and Lexical selection logic.\n- Supports element-scoped popup scrolling through `useVirtualizer`.\n- Supports measured row heights; useful when long repository paths wrap.\n- `scrollToIndex(selectedIndex)` can keep keyboard-highlighted option mounted and visible.\n- React 19 supported. Use `useFlushSync: false` per official React 19 guidance. [TanStack React docs](https://tanstack.com/virtual/latest/docs/framework/react/react-virtual)\n- Current package: `3.14.8`. [npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/%40tanstack/react-virtual)\n\nSuggested setup:\n\n```powershell\nnpm install @tanstack/react-virtual\n```\n\nUse:\n\n- Popup `List` as scroll element.\n- Virtualizer `count = options.length`.\n- Estimated row height plus `measureElement`.\n- Small `overscan`.\n- Effect calling `scrollToIndex(selectedIndex)`.\n- Render only `getVirtualItems()`.\n\nPrefer over `react-window`: TanStack integrates better with existing MUI markup and variable-height path rows. `react-window` v2 is more component-prescriptive and recently changed major API.\n\nImportant: virtualization fixes DOM overload only. Still must stop indexing ignored `node_modules` files and avoid creating 127k option objects while search inactive.\n\nVerification plan accepted: temporary large-index stress test, verify behavior/performance, then remove test. Keep ordinary fast behavior tests only. No changes made.\n\n",
